# Supply-chain agent

- Pin Node as an exact `package.json#engines.node`. Pin pnpm via Corepack `package.json#packageManager` sha512. Do not add `.nvmrc` or `engines` on workspace packages.
- Direct dependencies are exact versions in each `package.json` (no `^` / `~`). Transitive pins live in `pnpm-lock.yaml` and `pnpm-workspace.yaml#overrides`.
- Hardening lives in `pnpm-workspace.yaml` (pnpm v11+): `registry`, `saveExact`, `preferFrozenLockfile`, `allowBuilds`, `trustPolicy: no-downgrade`, `trustLockfile`, audit `overrides`.
- Lifecycle scripts only via `allowBuilds` whitelist. Do not widen without user approval.
- After override or pin changes: refresh lockfile deliberately, restore `trustPolicy: no-downgrade`, then `pnpm check:pnpm`.
- CI must keep `pnpm audit --prod --audit-level=high` failing the job (no silent `continue-on-error`).
